    "abstract": null,
    "field": "Global carbon cycle modeling",
    "problem": "Terrestrial biosphere models have large uncertainties in estimating gross primary productivity (GPP), which are critical for reliable carbon sink projections, and existing observational datasets have provided insufficient constraints to resolve discrepancies between models.",
    "method": "The authors propose a method to constrain modelled global carbon uptake by optimizing terrestrial biosphere model parameters using satellite-derived solar-induced chlorophyll fluorescence data, based on an assumed biome-specific linear relationship between fluorescence and gross primary productivity.",
    "task": "The task is to use satellite-derived solar-induced chlorophyll fluorescence data to optimize parameters in a terrestrial biosphere model and constrain its simulations of global gross carbon uptake.",
