    "innovation": "This paper demonstrates that using satellite-derived solar-induced chlorophyll fluorescence (SIF) data strongly constrains a terrestrial biosphere model, significantly reducing overestimated global gross carbon uptake, particularly in boreal forests, and bringing model estimates more in line with data-driven products.",
    "kg_extraction_triplets": [
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "ORCHIDEE",
            "source_entity_type": "Source",
            "relation": "PRODUCES_VARIABLE",
            "target_entity_instance": "gross primary productivity",
            "target_entity_type": "Variable",
            "paragraph": "Accurate terrestrial biosphere model (TBM) simulations of gross carbon uptake (gross primary productivity - GPP) are essential for reliable future terrestrial carbon sink projections. However, uncertainties in TBM GPP estimates remain. Newly-available satellite-derived sun-induced chlorophyll fluorescence (SIF) data offer a promising direction for addressing this issue by constraining regional-to-global scale modelled GPP. Here, we use monthly 0.5\u00b0 GOME-2 SIF data from 2007 to 2011 to optimise GPP parameters of the ORCHIDEE TBM.",
            "ontology_conformed": false,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "IPSL Earth System Model",
            "source_entity_type": "Source",
            "relation": "HAS_SOURCE_COMPONENT",
            "target_entity_instance": "ORCHIDEE",
            "target_entity_type": "SourceComponent",
            "paragraph": "ORCHIDEE is a global process-based terrestrial biosphere model (TBM) that calculates carbon, C, water and energy fluxes between the land surface and the atmosphere at a half-hourly time step39. It is the land surface component of the IPSL Earth System Model40.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
